  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: DiscS&E 2
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: 'A research team is working with human tumor cells and viruses that have
    been modified in the lab to study how potential cancer drugs might work.


    <b>The
    Institutional Biosafety Committee (IBC) reviews projects and provides safety
    guidance when certain materials are used, but it is not required to approve early
    discovery experiments.</b>


    Is this <b>true</b> or <b>false</b>?'
  explanation: "The IBC oversees projects that involve biological hazards, such as
    modified viruses or human cells, to ensure safety procedures are in place\u2014like
    using personal protective equipment (PPE), working in biosafety cabinets, and
    handling materials properly. As long as researchers follow the safety guidelines,
    they don\u2019t need separate approval from the IBC for each experiment in early
    discovery work. "
  correctAnswer: True
  incorrectAnswer1: False
  incorrectAnswer2: 
  incorrectAnswer3: 
  questionRole: Safety & Ethics
  questionType: TrueFalse
  questionStage: Discovery
